              <span class="text-xs font-mono font-semibold px-2.5 py-1 rounded bg-[#FAF8F5] dark:bg-[#1B2330] border border-[#E0DBD0] dark:border-[#263346] text-[#3368A0] dark:text-[#66A3BF]">Standard sRGB IEC</span>
            </div>
            <p class="text-sm text-[#475569] leading-relaxed">
              Discord clients render across a wide variety of hardware, from mobile OLED screens to desktop sRGB monitors. Assets exported in wide color gamuts such as Display P3 or Adobe RGB often appear desaturated or shifted when rendered inside Chromium-based desktop clients. For optimal color fidelity, all static and animated creator assets should be exported in standard sRGB with an 8-bit color depth. Additionally, preserving transparent Alpha channels in PNG files ensures emojis and role icons blend seamlessly across both Discord Dark and Light themes.
            </p>
            <div class="p-3.5 rounded-[10px] bg-[#FAF8F5] dark:bg-[#1B2330] border border-[#E0DBD0] dark:border-[#263346] flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 text-xs font-mono">
              <span class="text-[#6B7A90]">Target Gamut:</span>
              <span class="text-[#3368A0] dark:text-[#66A3BF] font-bold">sRGB (IEC 61966-2-1:1999) with 8-bit RGBA Channels</span>
            </div>
          </article>
        </div>

        <!-- Dossier Card 5: Client-Side Privacy -->
        <div class="dossier-sticky-wrapper sticky top-40 z-50 mb-8">
          <article class="card-panel p-6 sm:p-8 rounded-[18px] shadow-2xl border border-[#E0DBD0] dark:border-[#263346] bg-[#FFFFFF] dark:bg-[#141A24] space-y-4">
